# Rondo alla Turca, theme (repertoire plan: rondo-alla-turca). The opening eight bars of the
# A minor theme of Mozart's Rondo (Piano Sonata K. 331, third movement), the right-hand melody
# only, an octave below the piano, played twice as the composer repeats it. It starts with the turn
# B A G# A and the leap to C: the open string 2 (B), string 3 fret 2 (A), string 3 fret 1 (G#),
# string 2 fret 1 (C). The turns climb: around C, around E, twice around A, up to the top C; then
# the line falls C B A G#, A E F D, to the close C B A. The cadence (C, B, A) is written in plain
# quarter notes, without ornaments.
# Bar numbers here count the upbeat as bar 0 (the Player numbers it 1).
# Positions: first position for bars 1-2 (finger 4 for D# on string 2 fret 4); bar 3 shifts to
# fourth position on string 1 (finger 1 on fret 4: G#, 2 on 5: A, 4 on 7: B); bar 4 moves up to
# fifth position for the top C (finger 4 on fret 8); in bar 5 finger 1 slips back from A to G#;
# the open E in bar 6 brings the hand back to first position.
# Pick every sixteenth down-up (or alternate i and m), down on the beat.
title: Rondo alla Turca (theme)
composer: Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart
source: Piano Sonata in A major, K. 331 (1784), third movement, Alla Turca: the opening A minor theme, right-hand melody; arranged for guitar for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain (Mozart died in 1791); this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 6
tags: mozart, classical, sixteenth notes, turns, alternate picking, position shifts
tempo: 108
time: 2/4
key: Am
pickup: q

track: Melody
role: lead
